                 <item>
                  <widget class="QToolButton" name="toolButton_soilLookupInfo">
                   <property name="font">
                    <font>
                     <bold>true</bold>
                    </font>
                   </property>
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Lookup table (CSV or TXT):
- Mapping field: the column whose values match the categories of the input layer.
- Class field: the mHM soil class ID.
The horizons, either one row per horizon:
  HORIZON, UPPER_DEPTH and LOWER_DEPTH (mm), CLAY, SAND and SILT (%), BULK_DENSITY (g/cm3)
or one row per soil class:
  HORIZONS (count), then DEPTH1, CLAY1, SAND1, SILT1, BULK_DENSITY1, DEPTH2, ...
  (DEPTHn is the bottom of horizon n in mm)
Columns starting with * are ignored; a [unit] suffix in a column name is allowed.

Example (one row per horizon):
CODE,SOIL_ID,HORIZON,UPPER_DEPTH,LOWER_DEPTH,CLAY,SAND,SILT,BULK_DENSITY
12,1,1,0,300,20,45,35,1.35
12,1,2,300,1000,28,40,32,1.50</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="accessibleName">
                    <string>Soil lookup table</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="styleSheet">
                    <string notr="true">QToolButton { color: palette(link); }</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>i</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item>
