                 <item>
                  <widget class="QToolButton" name="toolButton_geologyLookupInfo">
                   <property name="font">
                    <font>
                     <bold>true</bold>
                    </font>
                   </property>
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Lookup table (CSV or TXT), one row per geology class:
- Mapping field: the column whose values match the categories of the input layer.
- Class field: the mHM geology class ID.
- KARSTIC: 1 (or yes) for a karstic class, else 0.
- PARAMETER_VALUE: the parameter set (an integer) the class uses.
- GEO_CLASS (optional): the geology parameter class; the class field when absent.
Columns starting with * are ignored; a [unit] suffix in a column name is allowed.

Example:
CODE,NAME,GEO_CLASS,KARSTIC,PARAMETER_VALUE
101,Sandstone,1,0,1
205,Limestone,2,1,2</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="accessibleName">
                    <string>Geology lookup table</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="styleSheet">
                    <string notr="true">QToolButton { color: palette(link); }</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>i</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
